Hi all,

while trying to fit some models I made a simple mistake:
I defined 100 000 iterations and 500 000 burn in samples instead of 50 000.
It took a while to figure out why nimble was freezing and in the end it was a simple additional 0  in the burn in.
Is it possible to add a warning to nimble and stop the computation when nburnin > niter ?
Because when this happens nimble freezes.

thanks
Rui

