Interestingly, this exact issue was raised to the nimble team not long ago by another user.  You're right, there was no checking for this case, and it could lead to a crashing of compiled execution.  In response, I added a check and a friendly error message, for exactly that case when (nburnin > niter).  This fix is already available on the development branch of nimble (on github, branch "devel"), and will be included as part of the next updated nimble package release.

Thanks for the comment and helpful feedback, Rui.

Daniel

